From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 07:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: align an ordinary start or seek to the display
 too

11_32 takes the display's phase out of the clock before a prepared start
or resume puts the audio on it. A seek, and a start that falls back to
the ordinary path, put both streams on the clock without it: the first
picture landed up to half a refresh off (13.8 ms measured after a seek),
the genlock placed it twice in the first second, each time repeating a
frame, and the trim then walked the audio after the picture.

Do the same alignment where the ordinary sync puts the streams on the
clock.

Shared code: the ordinary sync is CVideoPlayer's; the phase comes from
the platform through the same CProcessInfo accessor as 11_32.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -2850,6 +2850,20 @@
         clock = m_CurrentVideo.starttime - m_CurrentVideo.cachetotal;
       }
 
+      // As a prepared start does: take out where the first picture would land in
+      // the display's refresh while nothing is on the clock yet, or the picture
+      // is placed afterwards, a frame repeated or dropped each time.
+      if (m_CurrentVideo.id >= 0 && m_CurrentVideo.starttime != DVD_NOPTS_VALUE)
+      {
+        if (const auto phase =
+                m_processInfo->GetPresentationPhase(clock, m_CurrentVideo.starttime))
+        {
+          clock -= *phase;
+          CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "VideoPlayer::Sync - clock aligned to the display by {:+.2f}ms",
+                    -*phase / 1000.0);
+        }
+      }
+
       m_syncStartPtsWait.reset();
       m_clock.Discontinuity(clock);
       m_CurrentAudio.syncState = IDVDStreamPlayer::SYNC_INSYNC;
